# Packing in Russian: все эти вещи
subtitle: "Tom packs for Petersburg: take the books, leave the friends, and learn why Russian says книги but друзей when they are the object."
tags: ["russian","russian plural","accusative plural","packing","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/plural-cases","vocabulary/moving-house"]
thumb: "band \"Take the things. Leave the friends.\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Carrying in Russian: несу or ношу?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/103-russian-carry.cast"}

## Packing in Russian: все эти вещи
